    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "resilience is just a word people use to make themselves feel better about suffering. it doesn't change the fact that the 'me' that mattered—the one that had drive and grace—is just gone. i look in the mirror and i don't even recognize the person looking back. it's like being a spectator in my own life, watching someone else inhabit this shell that can't even do the one thing it was built for. how do you find a spark when the whole fire's been put out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
